+- `b`: Command-line argument `-b` controlling block size, default `DEFAULT_BLOCK_SIZE`, tested values 64, 128, 256 [S1, unofficial].
+- `blockDim3`: 3D block dimensions `dim3(8, 8, 8)`, resulting in 512 threads per block [S1, unofficial].
+- `gridDim3`: 3D grid dimensions calculated via ceiling division by 8 for each dimension [S1, unofficial].
+
+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
 - Memory allocation failure: If any `cudaMalloc` or `malloc` fails, the implementation must free all allocated resources (device memory, host memory, CUDA events) and return error code 1 [S1, unofficial].
+
+**Pseudocode:**
+```python
+def cuda_voxelize(mesh, opt):
+    # 1. Allocate device memory
+    verts_d = cuda_malloc(mesh.num_vertices * sizeof(float3))
+    faces_d = cuda_malloc(mesh.num_faces * sizeof(int3))
+    bounds_d = cuda_malloc(mesh.num_faces * sizeof(VoxelBounds))
+    grid_d = cuda_malloc(opt.res ** 3 * sizeof(unsigned int))
+
+    # 2. Copy host data to device
+    cuda_memcpy(verts_d, mesh.verts, cudaMemcpyHostToDevice)
+    cuda_memcpy(faces_d, mesh.faces, cudaMemcpyHostToDevice)
+    cuda_memcpy(bounds_d, mesh.face_bounds, cudaMemcpyHostToDevice)
+
+    # 3. Zero device grid
+    cuda_memset(grid_d, 0, opt.res ** 3 * sizeof(unsigned int))
+
+    # 4. Configure launch dimensions
+    block_dim = dim3(8, 8, 8)
+    grid_dim = dim3(
+        (opt.res + 7) // 8,
+        (opt.res + 7) // 8,
+        (opt.res + 7) // 8
+    )
+
+    # 5. Launch kernel and measure time
+    start_event = cuda_event_create()
+    stop_event = cuda_event_create()
+    cuda_event_record(start_event)
+    # Kernel body not provided in sources
+    voxelize_kernel[grid_dim, block_dim](verts_d, faces_d, bounds_d, mesh.num_faces, grid_d, opt.res)
+    cuda_event_record(stop_event)
+    cuda_event_synchronize(stop_event)
+    elapsed_ms = cuda_event_elapsed(start_event, stop_event)
+
+    # 6. Copy result back to host
+    total_voxels = opt.res ** 3
+    grid_h32 = cuda_malloc(total_voxels * sizeof(unsigned int))
+    cuda_memcpy(grid_h32, grid_d, total_voxels * sizeof(unsigned int), cudaMemcpyDeviceToHost)
+
+    # 7. Convert to binary
+    grid = [0] * total_voxels
+    for i in range(total_voxels):
+        grid[i] = 1 if grid_h32[i] != 0 else 0
+
+    # On failure, free all resources and return 1
+    return grid, elapsed_ms
+```
 
